**UI phase kicked off, 2026-07-19.** Backend fully done, so the UI phase started with `/design-consultation`: light-first "paper & ink" design system approved (not dark-first — ties to the "plain files, yours forever" pitch), dual-accent color system (vermillion=human-authored, teal=AI/MCP-touched, applied everywhere). Full detail in `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-19-ui-design-system.md` — that spec is the source of truth, this is just a pointer. **User-requested, explicit "remember this"**: real-time collaboration cursors must look like Figma's — colored per-user, username label under the cursor. Resolved design tension: teal is reserved exclusively for AI presence, so humans get a separate curated 5-color "ink" palette (vermillion/indigo/plum/ochre/forest), hashed per-user, cursor tapered toward a pen-nib rather than Figma's plain arrow. Implementation grounding: `y-codemirror.next`'s `yCollab` awareness protocol natively handles cursor position + color + name, no custom WebSocket tracking needed. New plugins installed for the UI build: `gsap-skills` (GreenSock official) and `frontend-design` (Anthropic official, anti-slop).

**Dependabot batching bug + full backend doc, 2026-07-19.** User flagged a "stuck PR" — #49 bundled 9 npm updates (the `dependencies` group had no `update-types` filter) and failed CI: typescript-eslint 8.64.0 crashes loading typescript 7.0.2 (real upstream incompatibility, not a code bug). Fixed `dependabot.yml` to group only minor/patch, so majors arrive as individual PRs — verified working: the batch immediately re-split into 5 real PRs, 4 merged clean alone, only the isolated typescript-7 one still failed (closed, waiting on upstream). While writing the doc, also found and fixed a real latent bug: `tree-sitter-javascript` was imported directly in `extraction.ts` but never declared in `server/package.json` — it only resolved because `tsx` (the app's only launch method) exposes pnpm's hoisted `node_modules` via `NODE_PATH`; a plain `node` run failed. Declared it explicitly, added the missing JS test case (TS/Python/Go each had one, JS didn't). Wrote `docs/agents/backend-reference.md` — full architecture, tech stack, data model, per-subsystem walkthrough, security posture, testing/deployment, single-process limitation, maintenance runbook — linked from README and STATE.md. 130 tests green, all on `dev`.
